  "description": "The free Community Edition of the SelectPdf HTML to PDF converter for .NET, free for personal and commercial use. Cross-platform: Linux x64 and ARM64, Docker images with no apt-get, Windows, and macOS on Apple Silicon. Built on a Chromium engine with full HTML5, CSS3, web fonts and JavaScript support. It offers most features of the professional converter; the main limitation is that it generates PDF documents up to 5 pages long. Features: convert any web page or raw HTML string to PDF, synchronously or asynchronously; page settings and resize-to-fit; document properties and viewer preferences; security (passwords, permissions, AES-256 encryption); PDF/A-1b to PDF/A-4 and PDF/X-1a output; custom headers and footers (including HTML) with page numbering; automatic and manual page breaks; HTTP headers, cookies, POST data, authentication, login forms and proxy; internal and external links; automatic bookmarks. Install a matching SelectPdf.Universal.Native runtime package (win-x64, win-x86, linux-x64, linux-arm64 or osx-arm64) for the Chromium engine. The Community Edition uses the SelectPdf.Universal namespace, the same as the full SelectPdf.Universal package, so moving up to it needs no code change; the full package adds output beyond 5 pages, PDF creation and editing, Word to PDF, HTML to image, redaction, digital signatures, form filling, PDF/UA and more.",
